# Staged by fisher-vls on 2026-11-26 for fisher-4h7.
# Acceptance from Stockfish 19 (sf_19, edb0d9d), Homebrew arm64 bottle,
# probed 2026-11-26: https://github.com/official-stockfish/Stockfish/releases/tag/sf_19
# Owner decision on fisher-4h7: over UCI, the file letter H grants the same
# kingside castling right as K on this position. See README.md for the
# source lines, the Stockfish captures and the move list below.
# Stockfish accepts this position and applies e1g1 with the same
# result as K. Without the right, e1g1 is illegal, and the owner decision
# for a rejected position sends one diagnostic before readyok.
> position fen 4k3/8/8/8/8/8/8/4K2R w H - 0 1 moves e1g1
> isready
# UCI isready/readyok, with no diagnostic before it.
< readyok
# The castled king on g1 and rook on f1 move on, and f1a1 checkmates
# Black. python-chess 1.11.2 and Stockfish 19 both report checkmate.
# A lost right, or a king or rook left elsewhere, makes a move illegal.
> position fen 4k3/8/8/8/8/8/8/4K2R w H - 0 1 moves e1g1 e8d8 g1f2 d8c8 f2e3 c8b7 e3d4 b7a6 d4c5 a6a5 f1a1
> go depth 1
# The owner approved this line on 2026-11-23 in a comment on fisher-2aj.2.
< info depth 0 score mate 0
# Owner-approved example for checkmate. UCI move format spells the null move 0000.
< bestmove 0000
# UCI quit.
> quit
! exit
